1327:D:/Projekty/TrinityTrack6000/MainControlBoard/Infineon/XMC4200/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * 		   Returned value should be masked with RDV0 and RDV1 bits to know the status. \n
1328:D:/Projekty/TrinityTrack6000/MainControlBoard/Infineon/XMC4200/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * 		   \b Range: @ref XMC_USIC_CH_RBUF_STATUS_DATA_VALID0, @ref XMC_USIC_CH_RBUF_STATUS_DATA_VALID
1329:D:/Projekty/TrinityTrack6000/MainControlBoard/Infineon/XMC4200/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  *
1330:D:/Projekty/TrinityTrack6000/MainControlBoard/Infineon/XMC4200/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * \par<b>Description</b><br>
1331:D:/Projekty/TrinityTrack6000/MainControlBoard/Infineon/XMC4200/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * Checks if RBUF0 and RBUF1 have valid unread data. \n\n
1332:D:/Projekty/TrinityTrack6000/MainControlBoard/Infineon/XMC4200/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * It checks the bits RDV0 and RDV1 of the RBUFSR register.
1333:D:/Projekty/TrinityTrack6000/MainControlBoard/Infineon/XMC4200/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * Returns the value of RBUFSR masked with bitmasks of RDV0 and RDV1.
1334:D:/Projekty/TrinityTrack6000/MainControlBoard/Infineon/XMC4200/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * It can be used to decide whether 2bytes has to be read from RBUF or 1 byte.
